WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.710
<i>Kazamatsuri, a quiet, peaceful 
city with greenery everywhere.</i>

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.200
<i>But, unbeknownst to all,</i>

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.430
<i>two major forces that divide the world in two</i>

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.850
<i>are locked in conflict beneath its surface.</i>

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.770
<i>Guardian, who seek to destroy the 
Key and keep the world as it is.</i>

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.670
<i>And Gaia, who want the 
Key to destroy the world.</i>

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.130
<i>I've infiltrated both groups as a member.</i>

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.470
<i>Having engaged with both</i>

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.730
<i>but belonging to neither as Suzuki Bondo,</i>

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:40.600
<i>I...</i>

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:43.540
Kagari, how about you and I

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.060
try preventing the planet's death?

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.690
That has always been my desire.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.380
<i>I'm here to fulfill my promise to the Key.</i>

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.100
<i>This is where it all begins.</i>

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.450
<i>I have a meeting with Gaia's 
Saint, Kashima Sakura.</i>

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.920
<i>She's the linchpin of the group's old guard, 
which is at odds with Suzaki.</i>

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.970
<i>Tricking her won't be easy.</i>

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.280
Come in.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:01.530
Episode 21
"Battle Behind the Scenes"

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.700
So, yeah, that's what's happening right now.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:00.920
I see.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.820
That's all you have to say?

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.380
Of course.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.580
You only get what I promised 
you as reward for your help.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.670
Reward?

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.100
If you help save this planet,

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.840
I will even fornicate with you, 
in the worst-case scenario.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.520
That's...

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:23.100
Is that Kotori?

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.890
Kotori is doing a fine job.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.050
The day she completes this thing,

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.730
she will rule over Earth.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.210
Is it just me, or are you 
getting dumber by the day?

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.860
That's not true.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.950
One monster can't do squat, 
no matter how strong it is.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.860
Just like how even the strongest 
superhuman can't destroy tanks.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.240
Tanks?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.650
Weapons that Homo sapiens use, right?

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.270
I just had a great idea.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.720
If tanks are stronger than superhumans,

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:53.870
then let us obtain one

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:59.380
<b>Super Kagari-chan 
Tank</b>

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.250
and use it to take over Earth.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.420
Kagari...

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.220
Why are you patting my head?

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.440
Out of pity.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.590
You were talking like 
someone with a feeble mind.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.020
Don't insult me.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.860
<i>I wasn't trying to.</i>

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.680
<i>I just want to do something of value.</i>

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.410
<i>Something somebody's got to do.</i>

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.040
<i>Like protecting my comrade's wish</i>

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.370
<i>and the home of those kids 
who called me family.</i>

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:37.630
A monster?

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:44.260
You're lost again?!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.640
Oh, you're out collecting insects?

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.760
Wait, those are monsters you caught!

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:50.460
Tch.

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:52.890
Excuse me.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.240
Coming.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.710
Nagai?

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.510
<i>Oh, she must've had her memories 
erased when she quit Guardian.</i>

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.230
Ah, never mind.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.680
I just found her in the forest.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.320
Thank you very much.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.200
She ran off the moment 
I took my eyes off her.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.910
Uh, sorry to ask,

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.830
but are you a member of Martel, too?

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:15.620
Yes.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.160
My name is Tsukuno.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.710
I've been working here lately.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.990
Is that so?

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.570
Akane-san, did you find any beetles?

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.930
Whoa, amazing!

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.940
You made a friend, huh? Good for you.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.320
<i>Nagai forgot who she used to be</i>

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.490
<i>and found a home for herself in Martel,</i>

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.700
<i>and for Senri Akane and that other girl, too.</i>

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:54.820
<i>Guess I'll go see Kotori's parents.</i>

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:58.670
Hello?

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.590
What? Right now?

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:11.880
The report you submitted the 
other day was very interesting.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.460
Thank you.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:17.170
By the way, I heard you met with Kashima.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.140
Right.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:23.010
Why didn't you mention that in your report?

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:25.310
I decided that mentioning any names

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:28.410
at this stage could be misleading.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.700
A model answer.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.200
What I hate most of all

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.500
is ignorant brats trying to pull one over me.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:41.920
Resist

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:41.920
Don't

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.290
Don't

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.270
Suzaki-san!

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.040
Y-You misunderstand!

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.670
Yes, I did meet Kashima Sakura, but...

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:50.780
<i>Very well.</i>

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:52.010
<i>I understand.</i>

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:56.480
<i>You prefer working under Suzaki.</i>

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:57.960
<i>I'm terribly sorry.</i>

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.060
<i>It's fine.</i>

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:02.230
<i>Believe it or not, I fully 
recognize how capable Suzaki is.</i>

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.230
Sounds like you were telling the truth.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.200
Takasago.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:09.400
Still, you were awfully honest with her.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:13.180
I didn't think I could trick her.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.570
True, she is a scary woman.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.170
Suzaki-san.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:20.380
What is the Key?

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:21.290
The Key?!

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:23.020
Where did you hear that?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.280
<i>Oh, right.</i>

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:27.090
<i>Here's a piece of advice for you.</i>

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.920
<i>If you wish to climb the 
ladder in the Suzaki faction,</i>

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.880
<i>you should approach the Key.</i>

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:32.800
<i>The Key?</i>

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:33.600
<i>Yes.</i>

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.310
<i>It's something they're chasing in secret,</i>

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.580
<i>even going as far as killing people...</i>

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.590
You're a greedy one.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:42.910
I like you.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.290
You want to know about the Key?

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.320
Yes.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.710
<i>Take away my eyesight if you want.</i>

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:59.080
<i>If I keep track of my 
steps and the direction,</i>

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.840
<i>I can figure out my current location.</i>

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.340
<i>We're below the temple now... 
The fifth underground floor?</i>

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.060
Welcome to the City of Stone.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.100
What is this place?

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:28.690
A compressed world that has existed 
alongside Kazamatsuri for ages.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.620
We call it the City of Stone.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:32.950
The City of Stone?

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:37.080
Simply put, it's like an alternate dimension.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:41.660
It was formed by the accumulation 
of a power imperceptible to humans,

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.330
or so some researchers say.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:45.620
Imperceptible?

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:48.040
Like the power to create monsters?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:48.980
Yes.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:53.830
You could see this entire 
city as one big monster.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.790
Just how big is it?

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:58.030
Not very.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:01.720
It's a copy of Kazamatsuri, 
but only a small part of it.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:05.880
And it lacks infrastructure, 
including power and water supply.

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:10.560
Still, it could be used 
as a shelter of sorts.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:14.230
It may have been built for that very purpose.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.520
If need be,

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.400
we could use a bit of several 
summoners' life forces

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.490
to build more.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:21.740
But that's...

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.490
I'm simply speaking of possibilities.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:28.170
Expanding it beyond this size 
isn't a realistic option.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.290
Kazamatsuri's "spirited away" incidents.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:34.880
Surely you've heard the rumors, too?

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.550
Well, yes.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.490
It seems this place was the cause.

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:42.560
This place is connected to Kazamatsuri

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.080
in ways others can't see, by being its copy.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:48.020
And sometimes it draws certain people in.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.110
Is that so?

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:53.260
Now, the most we can do is use those links

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:56.220
to transfer monsters between realms.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:02.160
The Key is basically a sensory 
organ the planet creates.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.390
It acts as the planet's eyes and ears.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:06.430
The massive planet

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:11.040
probably can't notice its 
own wounds otherwise.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.840
What will you do with the Key if you find it?

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.440
Earth is at its limit.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:19.310
If nothing changes, Kashima 
will get what she wants.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:21.430
The Key will destroy the world.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.510
Is there no way to avoid that?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:24.310
No.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:25.640
With that said,

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.830
where should we look for help?

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.800
Don't tell me...

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:32.960
You're really planning 
to use this as a shelter?

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.230
I had experts investigate.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:39.200
They said we could port 
a small ecosystem here.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:40.620
Even if the planet dies,

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.470
we can keep greenery alive here.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:44.450
And how many people could fit here?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:47.710
Less than a hundred thousand.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:48.840
With no infrastructure,

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.740
they'd have to return 
to a primitive lifestyle,

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:53.840
but we do have an argument 
that can convince them.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.440
Do you really have magic 
words that can do that?

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.780
Of course.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.470
All we need to say is,

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.720
"This is an artificial afterlife."

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.070
Hey, did you hear?

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:14.610
The usual Harvest Festa operation 
is canceled this year.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:15.710
Really?

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:19.490
Well, our friends aren't 
making any major moves,

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.470
and we're not doing anything, either.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:23.120
May I join you?

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:24.340
Whoa!

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:26.690
You're eating an awful lot 
again today, Esaka-san!

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:27.520
Yeah.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.400
I've been posted overseas.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:33.460
So my Japanese cake adventures 
are temporarily stalled.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.120
<i>For a while after that,</i>

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.840
<i>it was one peaceful day after another.</i>

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:41.340
<i>After Esaka-san moved overseas,</i>

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.970
<i>I took over management of his café.</i>

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:49.200
<i>And I kept living a double life as a 
member of both Gaia and Guardian.</i>

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:52.650
<i>Suzaki's artificial afterlife project</i>

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.980
<i>garnered a lot of resources, 
both human and financial.</i>

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.980
<i>He sold rights to live in the 
"afterlife" at exorbitant rates</i>

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.990
<i>and used those funds to 
develop the City of Stone.</i>

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.990
<i>As the City of Stone got 
closer to completion,</i>

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:10.770
<i>the Key became an indispensable 
trump card for Suzaki.</i>

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:13.750
<i>Gaia's split became a foregone conclusion.</i>

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.000
<i>Suzaki, who seeks survival 
in the artificial afterlife,</i>

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.720
<i>and Kashima Sakura, who seeks 
destruction at the Key's hands.</i>

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:22.650
<i>Beneath the surface,</i>

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.760
<i>the two were waging a cold war...</i>

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:28.810
<i>A harbinger of the impending conflict.</i>

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:37.840
Where's Kagari?

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:38.520
Went out.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.980
Again?

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.290
I tried to stop her, but she left anyway.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:47.530
Didn't you want to help Kagari as a Druid?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.080
There.

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:54.490
Go find Kagari!

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:57.620
I met them.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.920
Your parents.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.490
This might sound awful,

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.800
but those things aren't your parents anymore.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:06.930
They're monsters.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:09.760
You know that deep down, don't you?

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.650
That they won't come back to life.

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.270
You're wrong.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.970
Give it up already.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.730
Quit living like this.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.030
Your parents wouldn't have wanted this.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.340
Also, this job is dangerous.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:24.270
I know that.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.700
No, you don't.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:29.430
We're skating on really thin ice right now!

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:31.190
But if you just quit now,

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:33.500
you can go back to a normal life!

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.280
A normal life?

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.460
Without my mom and dad?!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.170
<i>I see.</i>

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.790
<i>She has nowhere to go back to.</i>

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.090
I refuse!

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:01.860
What do you hear?

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.610
All kinds of words.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:05.970
Is that how you learn language?

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:10.620
But, as much as I may have learned,

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.950
there's something I still don't understand.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:14.890
The human heart.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.120
I'm not surprised.

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:19.350
There is a massive gap

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:23.090
between your thoughts and actions.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.260
You hold the status quo very dearly,

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:32.340
and you never risk your current happiness 
in order to hold hope for the future.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.080
As long as you're content with the present,

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.170
you don't care what tomorrow may hold.

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:40.650
I find that thinking extremely disgraceful.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.460
But that's just what people are.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:46.440
We're all scared of facing reality.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.670
I fail to understand.

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:51.740
Oh, I just had a great idea.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.200
You should just put an end to class conflict.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.660
You make it sound so easy.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:15:01.540
<b>Super Kagari-chan 
Tank</b>

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:58.970
Assign roles in a much more 
efficient and rational manner,

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.540
and charge into the future!

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:03.750
What?

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.260
I just had to.

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.920
I don't like being patted on the head.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.180
Okay.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.220
I'll stop, but in return,

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.300
would you hold on to this?

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.510
Pick the one you like.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.980
I don't really get it,

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.880
but I feel like I'm being insulted.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.510
You're not.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.060
Then...

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:26.190
I'll take this one.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:27.380
If you have that,

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.940
I'll be able to tell where 
you are, even if you go out.

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:32.560
So keep it on you at all times.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.280
Very well.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.200
Anything for my great cause.

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:44.700
Do you know this Tsukuno woman?

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:45.960
No.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:49.920
She's a summoner Kashima 
recently picked as her protégé,

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:53.090
but it seems she used to be a hunter.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.260
Kashima Sakura's keeping a 
former hunter by her side?

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:58.070
Yeah.

00:15:58.070 --> 00:16:00.190
Isn't this a bit of a scandal?

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:02.400
No, a very grave state of affairs.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:06.480
Do you suspect Tsukuno of 
leaking the information?

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:11.820
She works at the House of Ties, 
a facility Martel officially runs.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:15.750
Kashima must've found her 
successor as Saint there.

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.740
We already have a good idea who.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.370
It's this girl.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:22.410
If she kept a traitor close at hand,

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.730
and then suddenly had 
her successor disappear,

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:29.000
how badly would that 
damage our great Saint?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.350
We'll do the finishing touches ourselves.

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:36.370
Pull this off, and it'll be 
much easier to promote you.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:37.390
What do you say?

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:38.600
Refuse

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:38.600
Accept

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:39.810
Accept

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:43.580
I accept.

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:48.400
Did they die?

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.530
<i>The plan will be put into action at once.</i>

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.660
<i>They must be holding an emergency 
meeting at HQ right now,</i>

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:02.410
<i>where Kashima Sakura will be condemned.</i>

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:07.420
<i>Suzaki already has the other executives 
attending the meeting in bed with him.</i>

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.670
<i>As soon as we receive word,</i>

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:12.920
<i>we'll capture Tsukuno and Akane.</i>

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:15.690
<i>They will never be heard from again.</i>

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.620
<i>All to further the artificial 
afterlife project.</i>

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:23.870
<i>You can't achieve anything without sacrifice.</i>

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:25.690
<i>So I'll...</i>

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.360
My fellow executives.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:31.010
Thank you so much for attending,

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:33.270
even though it's so late at night.

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:34.340
The thing is—

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.820
May I say something before we start?

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:38.270
Go ahead.

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:43.790
There's something I want to 
announce to you all tonight.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:47.080
I have chosen the next Saint.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:51.000
It's a girl named Senri Akane.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:55.870
Also, this will be the last time the 
title of Saint will ever be passed down.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.240
Well, Suzaki?

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:01.850
This decision should be 
quite agreeable to you, no?

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:07.040
I've already asked a woman 
named Tsukuno to guard Akane.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.100
She used to be a hunter,

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.100
but she is completely dyed 
in Martel colors now.

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:14.360
She's highly trustworthy.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.080
If you take this as a scandal,

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.110
I'm willing to retire immediately

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:23.180
and entrust Martel's future 
to Akane and you all.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.490
No, of course not!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.870
We need your leadership.

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:30.420
Hello?

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.620
<i>The operation is canceled.</i>

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:36.760
I don't need to explain why 
I called you here, do I?

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:55.440
I can trace the life force used 
in monsters that approach me.

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:59.030
Why did you save me?

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:02.660
Or was there perhaps someone 
else you wanted to save?

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.460
Why do you keep repeating such 
mistakes over and over again?

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:14.080
I won't make any excuses.

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.290
Why?

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:19.260
You know what will happen if 
the planet dies, don't you?

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:21.360
Even if I know it in my head,

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:22.470
my feelings,

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:23.800
my heart won't listen.

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:26.220
You probably can't understand,

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.010
but that's just how humans are.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.660
Disgraceful.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:30.600
Agreed.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.000
I have a question, Kotarou.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:39.020
Were you close to the individual you saved?

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:39.830
Nah.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.740
We're practically strangers.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.100
Then why?

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:48.050
Maybe because I don't want to lose any 
ties I have, no matter how trivial.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:52.000
What if the planet fell to ruin 
because of your trivial ties?

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:53.420
If it comes to that,

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.130
I'll accept ruin.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:00.450
You're awful!

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.880
Kagari, did you gain emotions?

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:09.720
Do you people lack even the will to survive?!

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:10.410
Kagari?

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.940
Why were you even born, then?!

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.640
The planet can't support 
re-evolution anymore,

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:17.990
but the remaining reserves, used wisely,

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:20.650
should be enough to produce fond memories!

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:22.350
And yet...

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:23.730
And yet!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:26.740
You've completely given up on surviving!

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:27.490
Kagari?

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:28.370
Hey, Kagari!

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:31.280
Life couldn't have

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.500
come into existence

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.150
to give up...

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:38.210
Kotori!

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.750
K-Kagari-san's...

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.090
The Key's...

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.840
Go back home!

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:45.230
I'll deal with this somehow!

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:45.680
But...

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.040
Just go!

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:52.370
Damn.

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:53.600
I can't get close to her like this.

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:04.280
<i>Oh, I get it now.</i>

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.250
<i>I...</i>

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:08.780
Kagari!

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:16.190
<i>Even if we know it in our heads,</i>

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:18.930
<i>our feelings, our hearts, won't listen.</i>

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:21.820
<i>That's just how humans are, Kagari.</i>

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:26.550
I have been shamed.

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:31.570
Why are you toying with me?

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:34.750
Kagari, I'm not helping you out

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:36.910
because I wanted to save 
the planet or anything!

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.110
It's because I was drawn to you!

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:41.570
Because I thought you'd give me,

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.050
Tennouji Kotarou, and not Suzuki Bondo,

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:47.230
a special place to belong!

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:47.860
Wha...

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.570
I fail to understand!

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:52.310
Are you saying you worship me?

00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:53.390
No!

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:54.970
When I say I was drawn to you,

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:56.120
I mean I love you!

00:21:56.350 --> 00:22:00.200
That's more humiliating than 
being marked with scent!

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:02.430
Stop humiliating me!

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:03.870
I can't.

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:05.170
Not anymore.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.760
Then I don't need your help.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:12.430
Remove yourself from my presence at once.

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:13.010
I refuse!

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:15.420
In that case...

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:20.170
I'll just have to leave myself.
